================================================================================
Marketing-oriented README rewrite
================================================================================

Context
-------
The top-level README mixed a one-line pitch with deep operational detail
(prerequisites, Lakebase grant tables, build-performance internals, per-domain
graph-engine keys). Reworked it into a marketing-first landing page that leads
with the value proposition and pushes technical depth to pointers into the
existing `documentation/` set.

Changes
-------
1. README.md
   - New hero + tagline ("Turn your Databricks tables into a living knowledge
     graph — in four clicks"), refreshed badges, and a "data semantics gap"
     opening drawn from documentation/product.md.
   - Benefit-framed sections: Why OntoBricks, the 4-click table, "What's inside"
     pillars (Design / Map / Build &amp; reason / Publish to AI / Govern /
     Pluggable engine), and "Runs entirely on your Databricks".
   - Condensed Get Started (local + deploy) with the full prerequisites and
     idempotent deploy checklist moved behind links to get-started.md and
     deployment.md. Dropped the verbose Lakebase grant tables, build-performance
     and managed-synced notes from the README (they live in
     lakebase-graphdb.md / graphdb-integration.md).
   - Added a Documentation hub block linking product.md, user-guide.md,
     features.md, architecture.md, api.md, mcp.md, lakebase-graphdb.md,
     import-export.md and development.md. Kept the databrickslabs Project
     Support disclaimer verbatim. Dropped the hard-coded version from the H1.

