================================================================================
Security: bump vulnerable dependencies (Dependabot)
================================================================================

Context
-------
Dependabot reported 16 open alerts on the default branch. Raised the security
floors and re-locked. The lockfile was regenerated through the internal proxy
(the only reachable index in this environment) and then host-normalized back to
`files.pythonhosted.org` — the proxy fronts identical `/packages/<hash>/<file>`
paths, so the URLs and hashes are byte-identical to a public-index lock. Verified
zero `pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com` URLs remain (deploy-safe per
`.cursor/09-package-management`).

Changes
-------
1. pyproject.toml
   - mlflow  >=3.11.1 → >=3.15.0  (critical)   → locked 3.15.1
   - gitpython >=3.1.55 → >=3.1.58 (high)       → locked 3.1.59
   - aiohttp  >=3.14.1 → >=3.14.3 (high+medium) → locked 3.14.3
   - sqlparse: new constraint >=0.6.0 (high, ReDoS; transitive) → locked 0.6.0
2. uv.lock
   - Regenerated for the above (and transitive mlflow-skinny / mlflow-tracing
     3.15.1). Host-normalized to files.pythonhosted.org.

Not applied (blocked upstream)
------------------------------
- cryptography: advisory patched in 50.0.0, but mlflow pins cryptography<50, so
  bumping makes the graph unsatisfiable. Kept at >=48.0.1 with a NOTE in
  pyproject.toml; revisit once mlflow relaxes the cap.

Modified files:
- pyproject.toml
- uv.lock
- changelogs/v0.8.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-08-28.log

